    "show_share": true,
    "description": "About 60,000 children - one in every 100 infants born in Pakistan every year - are born with congenital heart disease (CHD), sometimes referred to as a hole in the heart. Most of them do not survive beyond their first few years due to lack of awareness, and inadequate diagnostic and treatment facilities.",
